# Copy this file to `studio/.env` and fill in your real value.
# `.env` is git-ignored; `.env.example` is committed as a template.
#
# This file is for the LOCAL half of studio — the generation skills under
# .claude/skills/ that run inside Claude on your machine. The deployed half
# (backend/, frontend/) takes its configuration from Terraform and the deploy
# workflow, never from here.

# AWS access is NOT a key in this file. Sign in per session with `aws login`;
# the maintenance commands bridge those credentials to boto3 via
# `aws configure export-credentials`. Ordinary pipeline commands do not touch
# AWS at all — they go through the API. See docs/PIPELINE.md.
#
# This block used to name studio-prod-media-us-east-1 as "the media bucket".
# It is the PROD one, and local work runs against this machine's dev stack
# (#287). Do not copy that name back in here.

# Replicate API token — REQUIRED for the whole studio-* workflow. Every engine
# runs on Replicate: bytedance/seedance-2.0 (studio-media-seedance),
# kwaivgi/kling-v3-omni-video (studio-media-kling), and the image models
# google/nano-banana-pro | nano-banana-2 and openai/gpt-image-2 | gpt-image-1.5
# (studio-media-image).
#
# Assets are NEVER uploaded to Replicate: everything sent to a model must
# already be an S3 object and reaches Replicate only as a short-lived presigned
# URL. Upload a local file to S3 first (the `studio-media-s3` skill), then reference its key.
# Create a token at https://replicate.com/account/api-tokens
#
# **PUT THE TOKEN IN ~/.config/andreas-services/studio/dev.env INSTEAD** — the
# file that already holds this machine's dev pool password. That file is read
# FIRST, so moving the token there takes effect immediately and a line left
# behind here cannot shadow it. Leaving it here still works and always will;
# what the config dir buys is a secret that is not inside the working tree,
# where `git add -f`, a copied directory or a backup tool can all reach it and
# `.gitignore` stops none of them.
#
# The line below stays as a template for a checkout that has not moved yet.
REPLICATE_API_TOKEN=r8_your_token_here

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHICH STACK YOUR COMMANDS WRITE TO IS NOT IN THIS FILE ANY MORE.
#
# It is a PROFILE: `studio profile list`, `studio profile show`, and
# `studio --profile prod <command>` for one invocation against the deployed
# library. `dev-setup.sh` runs `studio profile sync dev` for you, and the
# profiles live in `~/.config/andreas-services/studio/config`.
#
# This block used to hold STUDIO_S3_BUCKET and STUDIO_CATALOG_TABLE, pinned
# here by `dev-setup.sh`. Two problems with that. A pin was per-CHECKOUT while
# the stack is per-MACHINE, so a second worktree had neither. And it covered
# two of the five values that select a stack — the API URL and both Cognito ids
# were only ever exported by `dev-up.sh`, into its own shell — so a `.env` and a
# shell could name different environments, with `catalog gc` reading the `.env`
# half and nothing printing either.
#
# **If your `.env` still sets either, delete the line.** It is read, and it wins
# whenever `--profile` is not given, so a stale one silently outranks the
# profile. `dev-setup.sh` warns about both; check with `studio profile show`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RETIRED VARIABLES. Listed, not deleted, because a line that quietly does
# nothing is exactly the failure the bucket rename was designed around — and
# `dev-setup.sh` warns about each of these for the same reason. If your .env
# sets any of them, DELETE THE LINE. None is read by anything.
#
#   XHARNESS_S3_BUCKET, XHARNESS_S3_PREFIX
#       The names before the August 2026 bucket rename, from when the pipeline
#       lived in its own repo. Renaming the variable alongside the bucket is
#       what made a stale pin inert instead of silently writing to the archive.
#       The old bucket has since been deleted — see studio/infra/README.md.
#
#   STUDIO_S3_PREFIX
#       Prepended to every key the CLI built. Removed rather than defaulted
#       (#303): the API owns the root prefix (STUDIO_MEDIA_ROOT_PREFIX), and two
#       authorities that merely happen to agree is the failure that removal
#       prevents. This used to add "only the layout migrator still reads it";
#       that command is deleted and now NOTHING reads it, which is why the entry
#       moved into the general list above rather than out of this file.
#
#   STUDIO_S3_MEDIA_PREFIX
#       The pre-restructure `media/` wrapper. Nothing has read it since the
#       bucket was flattened.
#
#   STUDIO_MAX_WALK_OBJECTS
#       Bounded the app's recursive reel over S3 objects. The reel enumerates
#       catalog rows now (#310) and STUDIO_MAX_FOLDER_OBJECTS bounds both.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Kling AI API 2.0 — OPTIONAL direct-API path for studio-media-kling. The default
# Kling path runs kwaivgi/kling-v3-omni-video on Replicate and needs only
# REPLICATE_API_TOKEN above; this key is for a deliberately purchased package.
# Create at https://kling.ai/dev/api-key (shown ONCE).
